      "text": "Aldol addition mechanism\n\nBase-catalysed addition of ethanal to itself: enolate formation, attack on a second carbonyl and protonation of the alkoxide to 3-hydroxybutanal.\n\nAldol addition of ethanal: 1 reactant(s) → 1 product(s), 4 states.\nStates: Reactants → Enolate → Alkoxide → Products.\nOverall ΔH = -10 kJ/mol; highest transition state 45 kJ/mol above the reactants (the rate-determining step is Enolate → Alkoxide).\nThe enolate (state 2) is the nucleophile; its attack on the second ethanal (the highest barrier) is the rate-determining step.",
